3	//! Postgres-backed `PolicyStore` (SeaORM). `put`/`delete` (SMA-446, Slice B Task B5) are
4	//! thin one-shot-`UnitOfWork` wrappers around [`PolicyStore::put_in`]/[`PolicyStore::
5	//! delete_in`] — the exact reference pattern `PgRoleGrantStore::grant`/`revoke` establish
6	//! over `grant_in`/`revoke_in` (B4): open a `SeaOrmTransaction`, drive the write on it,
7	//! commit, then best-effort bump. `put_in` validates the Cedar source against the embedded
8	//! schema before touching the database, and — like `delete_in` — rejects any mutation of an
9	//! existing `system = true` row (`AuthzError::SystemImmutable`); a *new* row with
10	//! `system = true` (the seeding path, Task 17) is not rejected, only edits/deletes of an
11	//! already-persisted system row are. `list_all` reads every row in one REPEATABLE READ
12	//! transaction so a concurrent write can't tear the snapshot (spec §6.2 challenge MINOR).
13	//! `put`/`delete` best-effort bump `policy_gen` via the shared `Generations` handle (spec
14	//! §7/D11: "bumped on any policy CRUD or role grant/revoke") — logged and swallowed on
15	//! error, mirroring `pg_organizations.rs::bump_entity_gen`: the write already committed, so
16	//! a Redis-down bump failure must never fail it, it just means the change lands on the policy
17	//! snapshot's TTL backstop (`policy_cache_ttl_secs + refresh_interval_secs`) instead of
18	//! immediately — the decision cache follows for free, since its key's policy component is the
19	//! compiled set's `content_hash` (SMA-470 D4), which rotates the moment that reload installs.
20	//!
21	//! `put_in`'s INSERT branch handles a unique-constraint violation via a SAVEPOINT (SMA-446
22	//! Slice B Task B5 — preserving the pre-Slice-B "abort whole txn, re-read on a fresh
23	//! connection" semantics WITHOUT the fresh connection): the INSERT runs on a nested SeaORM
24	//! transaction opened directly off the recovered `&DatabaseTransaction` via
25	//! `TransactionTrait::begin` (which only needs `&self` — deliberately NOT through
26	//! [`crate::adapters::persistence::uow::SeaOrmTransaction`]'s own `Transaction::savepoint`,
27	//! whose `&mut self` receiver `put_in`'s `&dyn Transaction` argument can't supply). A unique
28	//! violation rolls the savepoint back (`ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT`) — the caller's outer `tx`
29	//! stays alive and usable — then re-reads the row that won the race WITHIN that same outer
30	//! txn and compares content: SAME content (a concurrent cold-boot `reconcile_starter` race
31	//! between replicas inserting the identical starter policy, Task 17 follow-up) absorbs as
32	//! [`PutOutcome::AbsorbedIdempotent`], mirroring the same unique-violation absorption in
33	//! `PgSystemRoleReconciler::reconcile_role` (SMA-477, where `bootstrap.rs::seed_role_row` moved
34	//! when the role half grew a port of its own); DIFFERENT
35	//! content (two `PutPolicy` API callers racing to create the same `policy_id`) is a genuine
36	//! lost-update conflict and surfaces as `AuthzError::Conflict` — see the inline comments on
37	//! that branch. `put_in`/`delete_in` themselves never bump `policy_gen` (the caller's own
38	//! awaited, post-commit responsibility, and — for `put_in` — skipped entirely on
39	//! `AbsorbedIdempotent`, since the winning writer already bumped it for this row).
40	//!
41	//! SMA-477 adds a SECOND, boot-only write path on the same table:
42	//! [`SystemPolicyReconciler::reconcile_system`]. It deliberately does NOT go through `put_in`,
43	//! because `put_in`'s `SystemImmutable` guard is exactly what must keep holding for the public
44	//! `PutPolicy` API — a starter policy that changes with the action catalog can otherwise never
45	//! converge. `reconcile_system` opens its own transaction, `SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '5s'`
46	//! (this runs before the HTTP listener binds, so an unbounded lock wait is a startup hang with
47	//! no health endpoint to report it), takes the row lock, and hands the row to the pure
48	//! `authz::reconcile::classify_starter_policy`, which decides whether to seed, converge
49	//! silently, converge-and-report, or defer to a newer release. Only that path ever `Set`s
50	//! `content_fingerprint`/`starter_revision` — see `doc_to_model`'s own note on why they stay
51	//! `NotSet` for every operator-authored write.
52	
